# Tutorial 04 — the Cedar House starts: levels, then walls with thickness, height and justification.
title: Levels and walls
summary: Levels, walls with thickness, height and justification, wall types and joins
---
speed 18
open new
zoom window -3000,-3000 24500,13000
caption "Levels" "Every building element belongs to a level (storey)"
click panel Levels
wait 1.5
type LEVEL Rename "First Floor" "Upper Floor"
type LEVEL Elevation "Upper Floor" 3200
type LEVEL Height "Ground Floor" 3200
note "Ground Floor 0 – 3200, Upper Floor from 3200" at panel Levels for 3.5
wait 3
caption "Walls" "WALL draws a chain of joined walls; Thickness and Height are options"
type WALL Thickness 300 Height 6200 0,1500 6000,1500 6000,10000 0,10000 C
note "C closes the chain: the limestone wing" at 3000,10000 for 3
wait 3
caption "The cedar tower" "A taller chain: 7.2 m, joined to the wing"
type WALL Height 7200 6000,1500 6000,0 11000,0 11000,7500 6000,7500 ;
wait 1.5
caption "The entry wing" "3.3 m walls around the entrance and the kitchen"
type WALL Height 3300 11000,7500 11000,10000 21000,10000 21000,3200 11000,3200 ;
wait 1.5
caption "Justification" "Walls are drawn by their centre line, or their left or right face"
type WALL Justify Left 22500,0 22500,3000 ;
wait 1.5
type U
type WALL Justify Center
escape
caption "Wall types" "The Type option lists and edits layered wall types"
type WALL Type ?
escape
wait 2.5
caption "Partitions and joins" "A thin 120 mm partition T-joins the walls automatically"
type WALL Thickness 120 Height 3000 14600,3200 14600,10000 ;
zoom window 12500,2000 17500,11000
wait 2.5
zoom extents
type WALL Thickness 300 Height 6400 11200,5600 16200,5600 16200,10000 ;
caption "In 3D" "The walls with their heights"
click mode 3D
wait 1.5
orbit 60 4
wait 1
click mode 2D
caption "Next: doors and windows" "Tutorial 05 cuts the openings"
wait 3
